From 4e85973a4cd46fb6ce9002cb052f352c4c1e1b0a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hizuru254 <2654837056@qq.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 20:14:39 +0800
Subject: [02/14] protocol v1.4: pre-equilibration tooling and the
 non-stationarity verdict
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds tools/pre_equil.py (checkpointed regional-NVT pre-equilibration) and
tools/preeq_report.py (dPE/dt monitor), plus the experiments that show the
TBR drift is intrinsic to the model rather than to the initial state or flux.

Evidence (docs/STATUS_20261112.md §7):
  * 230 ps of 300 K pre-equilibration lowers PotEng by 2398 eV at a steady
    ~1 eV/ps, i.e. no plateau.
  * NEMD started from the 200 ps checkpoint still shows 54-57 % half-to-half
    TBR drift (same as without pre-equilibration).
  * Dropping the flux back to the canonical 1 eV/ps does not stabilise it
    either (24-61 % drift, +18..+22 K global heating).
  * Ti keeps dissolving into the Au film (700-790 atoms inside |z|<20 A), so
    every interface keeps roughening and the measured TBR grows with time
    (P350: 0.61e-9 at 60 ps -> 3.37e-9 at 200 ps).

Consequence: no trustworthy pattern ranking is possible with this model until
the interface is stabilised (real Ti-Si/Ti-Au potential, ns-scale
equilibration, or a lower measurement temperature). The earlier v1.3 claim
that 3 eV/ps improves the measurement is withdrawn here.
